# YAML file in Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# Used by GitHub, Zenodo, and citation tools to generate accurate citations.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this CITATION
  file) and the accompanying paper (see preferred-citation below).
type: software
title: "ftlm-gpu: GPU-accelerated finite-temperature Lanczos method for spin Hamiltonians"
abstract: >-
  Matrix-free GPU implementation of the Finite-Temperature Lanczos Method
  (FTLM) for isotropic spin Hamiltonians H = sum_c J_c s_i . s_j with an
  arbitrary list of pairwise couplings and arbitrary (mixed) local spins,
  with sector decomposition by total S^z and a block-Lanczos sweep over
  random vectors. Two state-to-index maps (compressed lookup table,
  combinatorial ranking) and selectable precision (FP64, FP32, FP16/BF16
  storage) on the GPU (CUDA); an OpenMP CPU path (FP64/FP32). Computes
  the heat capacity C(T), the magnetic susceptibility chi(T) and the
  effective partition function Z_eff(T). MATLAB (MEX) and Python (CuPy)
  front ends share the same CUDA kernels.
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-26"   # update on release
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ghasdeke/ftlm-gpu"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20378647"   # Zenodo archive; replace by the v2.0.0 version DOI on release
keywords:
  - Heisenberg model
  - spin cluster
  - mixed spins
  - Python
  - CuPy
  - exact diagonalization
  - Finite-Temperature Lanczos Method
  - block Lanczos
  - matrix-free
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - OpenMP
  - finite-temperature thermodynamics

authors:
  - family-names: "Ghassemi Tabrizi"
    given-names: "Shadan"
    affiliation: >-
      Technische Universitaet Dresden, and
      Helmholtz-Zentrum Dresden-Rossendorf
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"   # optional, fill in or remove

